<p style="margin:0 0 16px 0; font-size:16px; line-height:1.7; color:#232F3E;">The trajectory is unmistakable. In five months, the audience has expanded from bank operations to bank-plus-corporate, the operating model has shifted from downstream repair to point-of-entry validation, and the residual risk has been reframed from format compliance to <strong style="color:#232F3E;">data quality</strong>. That is the industry update.</p>

<p style="margin:0; font-size:16px; line-height:1.7; color:#232F3E;">Two modes remain compliant — fully structured and hybrid — and the unstructured one is going away on 14 November 2026. The interesting question for the next six months is not which mode you ship. It is whether the data inside that mode is good enough to clear point-of-entry validation.</p>
